# ======================================================================
# FRONTEND env example (React + Vite).
# Copy to `.env` for LOCAL DEV only. Never commit the real `.env`.
#
# ── PRODUCTION (Vercel) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Put these in the Vercel dashboard → Settings → Environment Variables.
# They are read at build time; Vercel redeploys after a change.
#
#   BACKEND_API_KEY
#       Server-only secret. MUST equal Render's AI_SERVICE_KEY.
#       The edge middleware (middleware.js) reads this and injects it as
#       `X-API-Key` on /api/chat/* before rewriting the request to the
#       Render backend. Missing → the middleware fails closed with HTTP 503
#       (by design).
#
#   ⚠️  NEVER set VITE_BACKEND_URL (or any VITE_*) in the Vercel env.
#       Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the public JS bundle.
#       Setting VITE_BACKEND_URL makes the browser call the Render backend
#       directly WITHOUT the X-API-Key header → HTTP 401 on /chat, and it
#       leaks the backend URL (and any VITE_API_KEY you set) into the
#       bundle. This is the #1 cause of the chat "401 Unauthorized".
#
# ── LOCAL DEV ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite dev proxies (/api/admin, /api/contact, /api/github) forward to the
# backend on :8001, so those work out of the box with `backend/` running:
#   cd backend && venv/bin/uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8001
#
# Only CHAT is not proxied: the browser calls VITE_BACKEND_URL directly, so
# run ai_service on :8000 too (auth is skipped in AI_ENV=development):
#   cd ai_service && venv/bin/uvicorn app:app --reload
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Chat backend connection (local dev only; keep unset in production) ---
VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000

# --- Build-time content source ---
# The production Vercel build must use the deployed backend. This is not a
# VITE_* variable and is never bundled into browser JavaScript.
CONTENT_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/content
# CONTENT_API_TIMEOUT=10
# CONTENT_API_ATTEMPTS=4

# Backend and AI service variables belong in their service-specific files:
#   backend/.env.example
#   ai_service/.env.example
# Do not copy server-only secrets into this frontend template.